-- title:
--   Completed stalk of the Γ₀(M')×Γ(ℓ) moduli ring is W₀[[t]]
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a prime $\ell\ge 3$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$. Two equivariance hypotheses are assumed: that `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ D` is preserved when a Weierstrass curve $W$ over any $A_0$-algebra $T$ and a level-$\ell$ datum $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ are moved by a variable change $C$ (the defining clauses being that both points satisfy the affine equation, that $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$, and that the two elements $\mathrm{indepElt}$ attached to $(x_P,x_Q)$ and $(x_Q,x_P)$ are units), and that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (namely `IsTwoKernel` when $p^k=2$ and `IsCyclicGenKernel p k` otherwise) is preserved when $h$ is transported by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k)`. Let $P$ be an abstract moduli package over $A_0$ for the rigid Weierstrass data whose level structure on an $A_0$-algebra $T$ consists of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant, a family of polynomials $h_p\in T[X]$ indexed by the prime divisors $p$ of $M'$ with `IsGamma0PowAt` at exponent $M'.\mathrm{factorization}(p)$, a level-$\ell$ datum satisfying `IsLevelPStructure`, and a trivial third component; thus $P$ provides an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ and a universal point $P.\mathrm{univ}$ in the quotient of raw such data by the variable-change relation over $B_0$, with the property that every point over every $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of $P.\mathrm{univ}$ under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0\to T$. Let $x$ be a raw datum over $B_0$ whose class is $P.\mathrm{univ}$. Let $R_0$ be a noetherian local $A_0$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, with an $A_0$-algebra map $\iota:B_0\to R_0$; let $k$ be a field in which $\ell$ and $M'$ are nonzero, and $\mathrm{res}_R:R_0\to k$ a surjective ring map with kernel the maximal ideal. Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0:W_0\to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal, together with algebra maps $A_0\to W_0\to R_0$ forming a scalar tower and compatible with the residue maps. Assume finally the factorisation clause: for every artinian local $W_0$- and $A_0$-algebra $T$ in the tower, every surjection $\mathrm{res}_T:T\to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal of $T$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, and every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi:B_0\to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T\circ\varphi=\mathrm{res}_R\circ\iota$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\Phi:R_0\to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T\circ\Phi=\mathrm{res}_R$ and $\Phi\circ\iota=\varphi$. The conclusion is that the type of $W_0$-algebra isomorphisms $R_0\simeq W_0[\![t]\!]$ is nonempty.
--
--   This is the formal-disc (étale-ness) statement for the moduli problem with $\Gamma_0$-structure of prime-power type at the primes dividing $M'$ and full level-$\ell$ structure: the completed local ring of the moduli ring at a closed point with residue field $k$, viewed over the unramified complete discrete valuation ring $W_0$ of residue characteristic $q$, is a one-variable power series ring over $W_0$. It is used to identify such completed stalks in the construction of the relevant deformation and Hecke rings, and is invoked in the variant where the power series ring is further adjoined a root.
